Every file in this directory (data/mri/) is derived from one person's public MRI scans, processed with the atlases
and templates listed in NOTICE.md at the repository root:

- the scans: the MyConnectome dataset, OpenNeuro ds000031, https://openneuro.org/datasets/ds000031, licence CC0
  (PDDL on the legacy OpenfMRI record). Required acknowledgement: "Data for the MyConnectome project were obtained
  from the OpenNeuro database (ds000031)"; also cite Poldrack et al. (2015), Long-term neural and physiological
  phenotyping of a single human, Nature Communications 6:8885, doi:10.1038/ncomms9885;
- Schaefer-200 parcellation, (c) 2016 Computational Brain Imaging Group (CBIG), MIT License;
- Harvard-Oxford subcortical structural atlas, distributed with FSL under CC BY-SA 4.0: t1/labels_t1.nii.gz is an
  adaptation of it, which is why this whole bundle is offered under CC BY-SA 4.0;
- ICBM 152 2009c template (the brain mask): Copyright (C) 1993-2004 Louis Collins, McConnell Brain Imaging Centre,
  Montreal Neurological Institute, McGill University; permission to use, copy, modify and distribute granted provided
  the copyright notice appears in all copies.

Changes made by the SUB-01 project: tractography and a 214-region connectivity matrix (connectome.npz, connectome_v2.npz),
atlas warped into the subject's anatomy (t1/labels_t1.nii.gz, atlas_names.json, region_volumes.json), skull-stripping and
resampling (t1/t1_brain_1mm.nii.gz, t1/brainmask_t1.nii.gz, t1/t1_to_dwi.npy), parcel-mean band-passed z-scored
resting-state time series (rest/*.npz, rest/qc.json), and a Hopf model fitted on half of those runs (slow_layer.npz).

The scanned person is anonymous and stays so: nothing in these files identifies them (no face, no skull, no name, no
demographics), and this repository must not add any name, link or metadata about them. The attribution above is the one
the dataset record requires; add nothing to it.

If you share these files or derivatives, keep this notice and license them under CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a compatible licence).
